From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris McLaughlin <19711592+qBitnaut@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 19:07:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] SL7 local: media: i2c: vd55g: Look up the privacy LED

The VD55G driver registers its subdev with v4l2_async_register_subdev(),
which does not look up the optional "privacy" LED that the V4L2 core
turns on while a sensor streams (v4l2_subdev_get_privacy_led(), called
only from v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor()). The OV02C10 uses the
sensor variant, so a "leds"/"led-names" pair on the VD55G node was
silently ignored.

Register the VD55G subdev with v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor(). The
extra work it does is parsing the optional flash-leds and lens-focus
references, which the SL7 does not set, so an empty notifier results,
the same as for the OV02C10. A privacy LED that is not bound yet defers
the probe, and the failure is reported with dev_err_probe() so that a
deferral does not log as an error.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate (SL7 local, but the change is generic)
---
 drivers/media/i2c/vd55g.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g.c b/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g.c
index 932877698946..1d4c3ec985b7 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g.c
@@ -2475,9 +2475,13 @@ static int vd55g_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 		goto err_power_off;
 	}

-	ret = v4l2_async_register_subdev(&sensor->sd);
+	/*
+	 * The sensor variant also looks up the optional "privacy" LED, which
+	 * the V4L2 core then turns on whenever the sensor streams.
+	 */
+	ret = v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor(&sensor->sd);
 	if (ret) {
-		dev_err(dev, "async subdev register failed %d\n", ret);
+		dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "async subdev register failed\n");
 		goto err_subdev;
 	}

